      "content": "The primary risk factors associated with storing high volumes of flammable industrial solvents in high-density racking systems include: (1) vapor accumulation due to the potential of solvents to release hazardous vapors into the atmosphere through degradation, patiency, or leakage, particularly when ignitable in air; (2) thermal runaway due to overlapping ignition sources from sources like sources sparks, overheated electrical equipment, and neighboring fires or malfunctions; and (3) structural integrity risk from accelerated degradation of materials under thermal stress.",
